One coworker is crouched roughly 1–2 meters ahead and below the wearer, beside several buckets. They mostly face the materials, briefly looking toward the wearer, but do not block access to the brick wall. The unfinished wall is immediately to the wearer’s right, while a mortar container and tools are within arm’s reach. Loose bricks and equipment occupy the floor, so the wearer should remain in place rather than step through the coworker’s work area.

The appropriate next action is to spread the nearby mixture evenly along the exposed mortar joints. This fits the unfinished masonry and allows coordination with the nearby coworker. Even application produces a consistent, professional finish.

